Subject: [PATCH] HID: playstation: leave non-state DualSense Bluetooth reports to hidraw

DualSense Bluetooth microphone packets use report ID 0x31 and the same
78-byte size and CRC as controller state. Their type nibble is 2 instead
of state type 1 (or the compatibility type 0). Parsing these as state
causes false buttons/touches, battery updates and microphone mute writes.

After CRC validation, skip controller-state parsing for non-state types.
Return success so HID core still delivers the report to hidraw clients.
This does not enable or alter Bluetooth audio on its own.

Experimental: not installed or hardware-validated. Prepared against the
Linux master source retrieved on 2026-10-23 from:
https://linux.googlesource.com/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/+/refs/heads/master/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
Kernel-file changes retain SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later.

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
@@ -1463,6 +1463,14 @@
 			return -EILSEQ;
 		}
 
+		/* Media packets share report ID 0x31 with controller state.
+		 * Leave them available to hidraw without interpreting audio as
+		 * buttons, touch contacts, battery status or microphone mute.
+		 * Some firmware uses type 0 for state; type 1 is the normal form.
+		 */
+		if ((data[1] & 0x0f) != 0 && (data[1] & 0x0f) != 1)
+			return 0;
+
 		ds_report = (struct dualsense_input_report *)&data[2];
 	} else {
 		hid_err(hdev, "Unhandled reportID=%d\n", report->id);
